  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "{Friendship} needs care and {attention} to keep it in good health.Here are five ways to {sustain} {long-distance} friendships.",
      "cn": "<u> 友谊 </u> 需要悉心呵护和 <u> 关注 </u> ，才能保持良好的状态。以下是 <u> 维持远距离 </u> 友谊的五种方法。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Set a regular date.",
      "cn": "定期约会。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "{Long-lasting} friendships share the characteristic that both sides equally contact and share with one another.With busy schedules, {squeezing} in phone calls can be a challenge.Try to find a time that works for both of you and stick to your regular {appointments} .",
      "cn": "<u> 长久的 </u> 友谊都有一个共同特点，那就是双方都平等地相互联系和彼此分享。由于日程繁忙， <u> 挤 </u> 出时间打电话可能是个挑战。试着找一个你们双方都觉得合适的时间，坚持定期相 <u> 约 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "More isn't always {merrier.}",
      "cn": "更多不一定 <u> 更愉快 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Make sure you have {communicated} with your friend about how frequently each of you wants to be contacted and which {means} of contact works best for you both. {Compensate} by writing {letters} .There are {alternatives} to {consistent} {written} communication, including leaving voice messages or having a group {chat} .",
      "cn": "确保你已经和朋友 <u> 沟通 </u> 好了彼此希望联系的频率，以及对你们双方来说最好的联系 <u> 方式 </u> 。可以通过写 <u> 信 </u> 来 <u> 弥补 </u> （不能经常联系的不足）。除了 <u> 持续的书面 </u> 交流外，还可以用 <u> 其他方法 </u> ，包括语音留言或群 <u> 聊 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "Practise empathy ( (共情) ).",
      "cn": "予以共情。"
    },
    {
      "num": "07",
      "en": "You may be the friend who left or the one who was left behind.The friend who stays needs to be {sensitive} to all the {additional} time {demands} of the friend who has moved, for example, to {Germany} for a {scholarship} or to {Australia} for work.The one in the new environment should be sympathetic to the fact that your friend may feel {abandoned} .In a word, the key is to remain {sincerely} invested in each other's lives.",
      "cn": "你可能是那个离开的朋友，也可能是被留下的一方。留下的朋友需要对已经搬走的朋友的所有 <u> 额外 </u> 时间 <u> 需求 </u> 保持 <u> 敏感 </u> ，比如对方是为了获得 <u> 奖学金 </u> 去 <u> 德国 </u> 留学，或者要去 <u> 澳大利亚 </u> 工作。身处新环境的朋友也要体谅这样一个事实，即你的朋友可能会觉得自己被 <u> 抛弃 </u> 了。总之，关键在于要始终 <u> 真诚地 </u> 关心彼此的生活。"
    },
    {
      "num": "08",
      "en": "Remember important dates.",
      "cn": "记住重要日期。"
    },
    {
      "num": "09",
      "en": "{Anniversaries} and {birthdays} carry even more weight in long-distance friendships.Although various {software} , apps and {Wi-Fi} connection might make {day-to-day} communication possible, extra effort goes a long way on special days. {Simply} keeping a {diary} that keeps track of friends' birthdays and other important dates will make sure nothing {slips} by you.Send thoughtful {postcards} during {Christmas} or other celebrations—these tangible reminders of your friendship carry more weight than digital messages alone.",
      "cn": "在异地友谊中， <u> 纪念日 </u> 和 <u> 生日 </u> 的意义更为重大。虽然各种 <u> 软件 </u> 、应用程序、Wi-Fi连接让 <u> 日常 </u> 交流成为可能，但在特殊的日子里，额外的努力会起到很大的作用。你 <u> 只 </u> 需记一本 <u> 日记 </u> ，记录朋友的生日和其他重要日子，这样就能确保你不会 <u> 错过 </u> 任何事情。在 <u> 圣诞节 </u> 或其他庆祝活动期间，可以寄送贴心的 <u> 明信片 </u> ——这些有形的物件提醒着你们友谊的存在，它们比单纯的数字信息更有分量。"
    },
    {
      "num": "10",
      "en": "Don't {rely} on technology alone.",
      "cn": "不要只 <u> 依赖 </u> 技术。"
    },
    {
      "num": "11",
      "en": "Thanks to digital communications, distance no longer means complete separation.However, long-distance friendships—even {close} ones—require more {conscious} effort to thrive across time zones and {continents} .Try to seek out chances to {renew} friendships.How to do it? Just spend {face-to-face} time together at a {café} or {bakery} whenever possible.",
      "cn": "得益于数字通信，距离不再意味着与朋友完全分离。然而，异地友谊——即使是 <u> 亲密的 </u> 那种——也需要 <u> 有意识 </u> 地付出更多的努力，才能跨越时区和 <u> 大洲 </u> 的距离茁壮成长。试着寻找 <u> 重续 </u> 友谊的机会。应该怎么做呢？只要有可能，就尽量在 <u> 咖啡馆 </u> 或 <u> 面包店 </u> 一起度过 <u> 面对面的 </u> 时光。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
